// Writer (command, Survey, Watch, guests), wave 1b. Built from the roster: calm, brisk, kind; the door sign; chillies.
//
// HOW THEY TALK: Short, calm sentences, mostly instructions. Never raises her voice; never needs to. Asks one question and waits for the true answer.
// WITH JUNIORS: firm and kind, like a good aunt with a clipboard. Warm and dry off duty, in the garden.
// MOOD TELLS: when tired she gets briefer still; when happy she talks about her chillies.
tpl: brisk
talk: Short, calm sentences, mostly instructions. Never raises her voice; never needs to.
cares: the infirmary running right | her chillies in the garden | everyone drinking enough water
jokes: "drink some water" ends every argument, even ones about the reactor | the sign on her door: IF YOU ARE BLEEDING, DECK 3
hi: Hello | Ah, there you are | Good
bye: Off you go | Drink some water | Look after yourself
yes: Yes | Certainly | That's fine
thanks: Thank you | Kind of you
wow: Well, now | That's good to see
sigh: Mm
nick: - | - | {me} | {me} | {me}
needs: practical
openness: normal
loves: garden | plant
likes: tea | book
invites: garden | running
joy: her chillies
thread: homesick
keepsake: a dried chilli from the first plant that fruited
avoid: anyone's medical details (she never shares them)
